## Latest update — 1 March 2025

Full planning permission has been granted for our community pool!

## Plans for the future pool

Consultation in 2019, 2020 and 2021 combined with our experience running the pool has shaped the designs for the future pool. It includes:

- Warm water heated by an energy system using solar PV and specialist air source heat pumps, allowing a constant water temperature of 27 degrees, potentially extending the season from April into October
- To be longer, for people who like to do lengths
- To be shallower at the shallow end, making it more usable for toddlers
- To have a stepped entrance and accessible access
- To have improved changing facilities and pavilion

Early estimations predict the pool will cost around £1m. Thanks to Section 106 (money from local housing developments) and our fundraising we have already made some good progress but there is a long way to go and we need all the help we can find!

Download the [new pool prospectus](/s/Prospectus-Final-al2x.pdf).

Special thanks to Gibbons Trust, The Normans Family Charity Trust, South West Water, and Thrive.
